{"id":"167756","created":"1981-09-01T00:00:00+00:00","revision_id":96,"metadata":{"citation_count":37,"publication_info":[{"year":1983,"artid":"162","page_start":"162","journal_title":"Annals Phys.","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214855"},"journal_volume":"145"}],"report_numbers":[{"value":"NUB-2526"},{"value":"IFP-160-UNC"}],"citation_count_without_self_citations":35,"core":true,"dois":[{"value":"10.1016/0003-4916(83)90176-8"}],"titles":[{"title":"Tensor Methods for the Exceptional Group E6"},{"title":"TENSOR METHODS FOR THE EXCEPTIONAL GROUP E6"}],"$schema":"https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json","authors":[{"uuid":"f7dfc9d1-be83-4152-99c0-db1ea4562c05","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1003217"},"full_name":"Kephart, Thomas W.","affiliations":[{"value":"Northeastern U.","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/903081"}}],"signature_block":"CAFADt"},{"uuid":"655e99a5-5989-4eb9-95ac-f15f19e955af","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/984903"},"full_name":"Vaughn, Michael T.","affiliations":[{"value":"Northeastern U.","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/903081"}}],"signature_block":"VAGHNm","curated_relation":true}],"curated":true,"texkeys":["Kephart:1981gf"],"citeable":true,"keywords":[{"value":"GAUGE FIELD THEORY: group: exceptional","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"GROUP THEORY: REPRESENTATION","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"FIELD THEORY: SCALAR","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"POSTULATED PARTICLE: HIGGS PARTICLE","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"MODEL: HIGGS","schema":"INSPIRE"}],"refereed":true,"abstracts":[{"value":"We present a tensor formalism to describe irreducible representations of the exceptional group E 6 . Irreducible tensors are characterized by covariant and contravariant indices associated with the irreducible representation 27 , and a third (orthogonal-type) index associated with the 78 ; contractions of these indices with a set of invariant tensors are required to vanish for irreducibility. The formalism is applied to the reduction of Kronecker products of E 6 irreducible representations. As a further illustration of the method, we construct explicitly the Higgs potential for scalar fields in the E 6 representations 27, 78, 351, 351′ .","source":"Elsevier"}],"references":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/92111"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"438","page_start":"438","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.Lett.","journal_volume":"32"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/155747"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"185","page_start":"185","journal_title":"Phys.Rept.","journal_volume":"72"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/100124"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"177","page_start":"177","journal_title":"Phys.Lett.B","journal_volume":"60"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/6195"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"28","page_start":"28","journal_title":"Lett.Nuovo Cim.","journal_volume":"21"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/130994"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"389","page_start":"389","journal_title":"Phys.Lett.B","journal_volume":"77"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1429721"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"30","page_start":"30","journal_title":"Phys.Lett.B","journal_volume":"79"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/7907"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"388","page_start":"388","journal_title":"Nucl.Phys.B","journal_volume":"161"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/121698"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"5","page_start":"5","journal_title":"Lett.Nuovo Cim.","journal_volume":"